  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal, by means of its design, scale and siting, would appear incongruous and contrived with the built form, character, and distinctiveness of the Becontree Estate. Its irregular form and non-rectilinear shape, along with the cumulative impact of the existing extension would lead to harm to the character and appearance of the host dwelling and wider area.&nbsp; The proposal would cause undue harm to the character of the host dwelling, and harm to the non-designated heritage asset. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to preserve and enhance these key features:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policy HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021) The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012) Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4&nbsp;and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
